    transient_scope_untrack_skipped_cross_thread_or_borrowed_2026-11-26, P3, open, "Rust runtime transient-scope untrack skips frees on another thread, while the scope slot is borrowed, or via raw dealloc", doc/08_tracking/bug/native_build_hir_sigsegv_under_20g_cgroup_cuda_port_closure_2026-11-22.md, 1, doc/08_tracking/bug/native_build_hir_sigsegv_under_20g_cgroup_cuda_port_closure_2026-11-22.md, 2026-11-26, 2026-11-26, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    transient_scope_untrack_skipped_cross_thread_or_borrowed_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-26 filed from native_build_hir_sigsegv_under_20g_cgroup_cuda_port_closure_2026-11-22 (fix 22fb17305f0): the Rust runtime untrack hook (collections::transient_untrack_freed_addr, called from unregister_heap_ptr*) still skips three free cases: a free on a thread other than the scope owner (scope is thread-local), a free while this thread's scope/session slot is borrowed (try_borrow_mut declines), and raw dealloc that bypasses unregister_heap_ptr*. Each leaves a stale scope entry; address reuse by a paused-born object would be freed at scope end, and a duplicate makes the scope index ambiguous so every later untrack in that scope is an O(n) scan. Not reproduced; found by code reading."

